Simplified text: Auditing Accounts – Section 44 of Administrators General Act, 1963
44. State Government Reporting Requirements:

The auditors are responsible for reviewing the accounts. They must submit a statement to the State Government in the required format, along with a report and a signed certificate stating:
(a) if the accounts were audited according to the regulations;
(b) whether the accounts provide a complete and accurate record of all necessary information;
(c) if the Administrator-General maintained the required books as per the Act's rules;
(d) if assets and securities were handled and invested as directed by the Act or its rules, or if there are any deficiencies or failures to comply with the Act or rules, as specified in the certificate.

