Simplified text: Security for Good Behavior:
When an Executive Magistrate learns about someone in their area who is spreading seditious material intentionally, either verbally, in writing, or in any other way, such as:
Content punishable under particular sections of the Indian Penal Code;
Content concerning intimidation or defamation of a Judge in their official capacity under the Indian Penal Code;
Obscene material specified in the Indian Penal Code;
If the Magistrate has reason to believe there is a case, they can require the individual to explain why they should not be asked to sign a bond for good behavior for up to one year, possibly with guarantors.
Not applicable to registered publications following the Press and Registration of Books Act, 1867, without authorization from the State Government or designated officer.

